sw: estimated pagination places the pages once per layout action.

With estimated pagination (large plain text, large DOCX) the layout removes the surplus estimated
pages as it goes. Every removal repositions all following pages and moves their frames
(SwRootFrame::CheckViewLayout, lcl_MoveAllLowers), once per CheckPageDescs: at about 100,000 pages
(docx-text 50 MB) a quarter of the layout time.

Complete and idle layout actions take no shortcut by visible area, so the page positions are now
computed once when the action's page loop ends (SwViewLayoutDeferGuard, a no-op without estimated
pagination), before the interrupt formatting that looks for pages by position.

Hook: sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx.
Test: CppunitTest_sw_core_layout testLargeDocxPaginationUnchanged / testLargeTextPaginationUnchanged
(every page starts at the same text as the layout without estimates).
---
--- a/sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 
 #include <ctime>
 #include <rootfrm.hxx>
+#include <optional>
 #include <rowfrm.hxx>
 #include <pagefrm.hxx>
 #include <viewimp.hxx>
@@ -523,6 +524,12 @@
         return bAgain;
     };
 
+    // HST: estimated pagination removes and inserts pages all along the layout; place the pages
